# Pin Python source to LF regardless of the user's `core.autocrlf` setting.
# 13 tracked tests and runtime modules compute SHA256 fingerprints over
# `Path(...).read_bytes()` of `.py` files (see `tests/test_memory_grounding_contract.py:92-95`
# as a representative case). On Windows clones with the default
# `core.autocrlf=true`, git would convert `\n` → `\r\n` at checkout time,
# producing a different byte stream and a different SHA than the fixture
# pin, failing the fingerprint tests on fresh clone. `* text=auto eol=lf`
# forces consistent LF on checkout across platforms.
*.py text eol=lf
